==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Maid SP''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is an interesting take on [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]], with Cat Maid having a similar build but different tools at her disposal. Both have an emphasis on strong base damage while being easy to replace in battle.

Despite both having about the same base damage, Cats in the Cradle's attacks always produce [[Wave Attack|Waves]], effectively giving him pierce and twice the damage of Cat Maid against most enemies. This makes Cat Maid's generalist damage pale in comparison, and even more considering that other nukers like [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Thundia β]] also have better base damage.

Cat Maid's advantage over Cats in the Cradle, however, is her trait and debuff immunity abilities, especially [[Massive Damage]] to two traits. Floating and Zombie enemies are often melee enemies—precisely the type of enemy vulnerable to Cat Maid's 200k effective damage at level 30. For Zombie enemies, Cat Maid's immunities can be convenient against enemies like [[Zir Zeal]] attempting to impede her, and another Cat Maid can quickly be spawned for tough zombies who got past the preceding one. Peons may bait attacks from her, so it's important to time her correctly. Floating enemy counters may be crowded, but Cat Maid has not much of an issue defeating many of them, whether they be [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants or debuffer midrangers such as [[Maawth]] or [[I.M. Phace]]. While Cats in the Cradle is an all-around nuker, Cat Maid competes by focusing on specialist values.

